Modifications (port to Lean v4.35.0-rc3 / Mathlib ec6a61cec0d8f9fda04453e9bb5761a79aa43a70)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Declaration names, namespaces and statements are unchanged. Changes:
1. Every import `SLT.X` was rewritten to `SharpSymmetricLSI.Vendor.SLT.X`; files placed at the
   corresponding paths under this directory.
2. EfronStein.lean, `condExpExceptCoord_stronglyMeasurable`: `measurable_pi_lambda _ (fun j => …)`
   replaced by `measurable_pi_iff.2 (fun j => …)` (Mathlib signature change).
3. GaussianPoincare/EfronSteinApp.lean, `rademacher_values_ae`: `AEMeasurable.of_map_ne_zero` no
   longer exists, and `Measure.map` of a non-a.e.-measurable function is now a Dirac mass (for a
   nonzero measure) rather than `0`. The a.e.-measurability of `ε` is re-proved: the zero
   measure case contradicts `IsProbabilityMeasure rademacherMeasure`; otherwise a Dirac mass
   would equal `rademacherMeasure`, contradicted by evaluating on `{1}` and `{-1}`.
4. GaussianPoincare/Limit.lean, `rademacherLaw`: `Measure.isProbabilityMeasure_map …` replaced by
   `inferInstance` (push-forwards of probability measures are now probability measures by
   instance).
5. GaussianLSI/BernoulliLSI.lean, `bernoulli_flip_invariance`: `Measure.map_smul` now takes an
   `AEMeasurable` argument; supplied as `(measurable_of_finite (flipCoord j)).aemeasurable`.

No `sorry`, `admit`, `native_decide` or `axiom` declarations; the main theorem depends only on
`propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.
